    "document": "Media_Composer_Editing_Guide_2024.x.pdf",
    "page": 1243,
    "chunk": 1,
    "text": "1243\nHD Formats and Resolutions\nIn the following tables, both Sony and Panasonic support some of the same AVC Long GOP resolutions. If\nan AVC Long GOP resolution is supported by both Sony and Panasonic, choose the applicable Video\nResolution Encoding Profile in the Media Creation dialog. Note the following:\nl If the resolution is listed with an asterisk (*) it is not available for Capture.\nl If the resolution is listed with a plus sign (+) it is not available for OP1a Media Creation.\nn The Panasonic encoding profiles appear as Panasonic AVC Long- GOP and the Sony encoding profiles\nappear as XAVC-L HD.\nn For 1080p/50 and 1080p/59.94 projects, the AVC Long G formats that appear for Media Creation in\nMedia Composer are listed as AVC Long GOP 12 and AVC Long GOP 50. Technically these formats are\nactually AVC Long GOP 6 and AVC Long GOP 25. According to the Panasonic specification, the bit\nrates for the 1080p/50 and 1080p/59.94 projects are 2x. Therefore you will see AVC Long GOP 6 as\nAVC Long GOP 12 and AVC Long GOP 25 as Long GOP 50.\nProject Format\nRaster Dimension\nFrame Rate\nResolutions\nHD\nHD 1080i\n1920 x 1080\n50\nYCbCR 709 Color Space:\nl\nAVC Intra 100\nl\nXAVC Intra 100 *\nl\nDNxHD SQ *\nl\nDNxHD HQ *\nl\nDNxHD HQX *\nl\nDVCPro HD *\nl\nJ2K 1080i 50 +\nl\nH.264 800Kbps Proxy *, +\nl\nH.264 2.0Mbps Proxy *, +\nl\nXDCAM EX 35 Mbits *\nl\nXDCAM HD 50Mbits *\nl\n1:1 *, +\nl\n1:1 10 bit *, +\nl\nDNxUncompressed 4:2:2 8bit\n*\nl\nDNxUncompressed 4:2:2 10bit\n*\nl\nDNxUncompressed 4:2:2 12bit\n*\nl\nDNxUncompressed 4:2:2\n32bit float *\nl\nAVC Long GOP 6 *\nl\nAVC Long GOP 12 *\n35 Project Formats and Resolutions"
  },
